  "configuration_id": "config_002",
  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the first experiment should establish a high-ceiling baseline using the most sophisticated components across all design axes: multimodal (both modalities), multiprofile (richer cellular context), scgpt (learned, biologically-informed RNA encoder), imagenet_vit_l (large pretrained image encoder), transformer aggregation (attention-based profile pooling), and weighted fusion (learned modality combination). This configuration tests whether the full pipeline can achieve strong validation accuracy and provides a reference upper bound. Subsequent experiments can then ablate individual components (e.g., swap scgpt→pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l→resnet50, transformer→avgpool) to identify which design choices drive performance, making this the most informative first probe under the 10-experiment budget."
}

